{{Elections in Alabama}}
The '''2024 United States House of Representatives elections in Alabama''' were held on November 5, 2024, to elect the seven [[United States House of Representatives|U.S. representatives]] from the [[U.S. state|state]] of [[Alabama]], one from each of the state's seven [[Alabama's congressional districts|congressional districts]]. The elections coincided with the [[2024 United States presidential election|2024 U.S. presidential election]], as well as [[2024 United States House of Representatives elections|other elections]] to the House of Representatives, [[2024 United States Senate elections|elections]] to the [[United States Senate]], and various [[2024 United States elections|state and local elections]].

Candidate qualifying for both major parties ended on November 10, 2023. Primary elections were held on March 5, 2024, as Alabama was a [[Super Tuesday]] state in the presidential election calendar.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://altoday.com/archives/53817-gop-candidate-qualifying-opens-on-october-16|title=GOP candidate qualifying opens on October 16|last=Moseley|first=Brandon|work=Alabama Today|date=September 12, 2023|access-date=November 6, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231106200454/https://altoday.com/archives/53817-gop-candidate-qualifying-opens-on-october-16|archive-date=November 6, 2023|url-status=dead}}</ref> In races where no candidate received over 50% in a primary, runoff elections occurred on April 16, 2024;<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.wvtm13.com/article/election-day-2024-alabama-primary/45769269|title=Alabama 2024 Primary Election: Races, registration and important dates|last=Reitz|first=Ian|work=WVTM-13|date=November 7, 2023|access-date=November 10, 2023}}</ref> this occurred in both the Democratic and Republican primaries in [[Alabama's 2nd congressional district]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.al.com/news/2024/03/brewbaker-advances-to-runoff-in-gop-race-in-alabamas-new-2nd-district.html|title=Brewbaker advances to runoff in GOP race in Alabama's new 2nd District|last=Cason|first=Mike|work=AL.com|date=March 5, 2024|access-date=March 5, 2024}}</ref>
