{{see also|Alabama's 1st congressional district}}
Under the new congressional map, the 1st congressional district encompasses the southernmost parts of the state, including all of [[Baldwin County, Alabama|Baldwin]], [[Coffee County, Alabama|Coffee]], [[Covington County, Alabama|Covington]], [[Dale County, Alabama|Dale]], and [[Escambia County, Alabama|Escambia]] counties, including the cities of [[Bay Minette, Alabama|Bay Minette]], [[Daphne, Alabama|Daphne]], [[Enterprise, Alabama|Enterprise]] and [[Ozark, Alabama|Ozark]].<ref name="ALT2">{{Cite web|url=https://altoday.com/archives/54149-terri-sewell-applauds-new-special-master-drawn-congressional-maps|title=Terri Sewell applauds new special master drawn congressional maps|last=Moseley|first=Brandon|work=Alabama Today|date=September 26, 2023|access-date=September 27, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231021170547/https://altoday.com/archives/54149-terri-sewell-applauds-new-special-master-drawn-congressional-maps|archive-date=October 21, 2023|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref name="ALcom2">{{Cite web|url=https://www.al.com/news/2023/09/court-ordered-alabama-congressional-maps-add-2nd-opportunity-district-for-black-voters.html|title=Court-ordered Alabama congressional maps add 2nd opportunity district for Black voters|last=Cason|first=Mike|work=AL.com|date=September 26, 2023|access-date=September 27, 2023}}</ref> It also includes whiter parts of [[Mobile County, Alabama|Mobile County]] and the city of [[Mobile, Alabama|Mobile]]. Incumbent Republican [[Jerry Carl]] had been re-elected with 84.2% of the vote in 2022 against a [[Libertarian Party (United States)|Libertarian]] candidate.<ref name="HPVT">{{cite web|url=https://www.cookpolitical.com/charts/house-charts/national-house-vote-tracker/2022|title=2022 National House Vote Tracker|access-date=October 17, 2023|website=[[The Cook Political Report with Amy Walter|Cook Political Report]]}}</ref>

Following redistricting, [[Alabama's 2nd congressional district|2nd district]] incumbent [[Barry Moore (American politician)|Barry Moore]] was placed into the 1st district as well, setting up a primary between Moore and Carl, both incumbents.<ref name="CarlRE">{{Cite web|url=https://yellowhammernews.com/carl-announces-reelection-bid-after-fed-proposed-map-signals-primary-with-moore/|title=Carl announces reelection bid after Fed-proposed map signals primary with Moore|last=Everett|first=Grayson|work=Yellowhammer News|date=September 26, 2023|access-date=September 26, 2023}}</ref> On October 30, 2023, Moore confirmed to ''[[1819 News]]'' that he would run in the first congressional district, challenging Carl in the Republican primary.<ref name="MooreFirst">{{Cite web|url=https://1819news.com/news/item/barry-moore-to-challenge-jerry-carl-for-district-1-seat-i-am-a-true-conservative-and-the-system-doesnt-like-a-true-conservative|title=Barry Moore to challenge Jerry Carl for District 1 seat: 'I am a true conservative, and the system doesn't like a true conservative'|last=Taylor|first=Caleb|work=[[1819 News]]|date=October 30, 2023|access-date=October 30, 2023}}</ref>

