{{see also|Alabama's 2nd congressional district}}
In the new congressional map, the 2nd district encompasses all of [[Montgomery County, Alabama|Montgomery County]] and the capital city of [[Montgomery, Alabama|Montgomery]], as well as majority Black sections of the [[Wiregrass (region)|Wiregrass Region]] and the city of Mobile. It also includes the entirety of [[Butler County, Alabama|Butler]], [[Macon County, Alabama|Macon]], [[Monroe County, Alabama|Monroe]], [[Pike County, Alabama|Pike]], and [[Russell County, Alabama|Russell]] counties, including the cities of [[Greenville, Alabama|Greenville]], [[Monroeville, Alabama|Monroeville]], [[Troy, Alabama|Troy]], and [[Tuskegee, Alabama|Tuskegee]].<ref name="ALT2" /><ref name="ALcom2" /> The district is currently represented by Republican [[Barry Moore (American politician)|Barry Moore]], who was re-elected with 69.12% of the vote in 2022; however, Moore's home county of Coffee was drawn out of the 2nd district and into the first. This left the district with no incumbent, as Moore instead chose to run in the 1st district.<ref name="HPVT"/><ref name="CarlRE" />

