{{see also|Alabama's 3rd congressional district}}
The 3rd district is based in eastern Alabama, taking in [[Calhoun County, Alabama|Calhoun]], [[Etowah County, Alabama|Etowah]], [[Lee County, Alabama|Lee]], and [[Talladega County, Alabama|Talladega]] counties, including the cities of [[Anniston, Alabama|Anniston]], [[Auburn, Alabama|Auburn]], [[Gadsden, Alabama|Gadsden]], and [[Talladega, Alabama|Talladega]]. The incumbent is Republican [[Mike Rogers (Alabama politician)|Mike Rogers]], who was re-elected with 71.3% of the vote in 2022.<ref name="HPVT"/>

Rogers has qualified to run for reelection. Rogers faced criticism from conservative colleagues over his initial refusal to support [[Jim Jordan]] in the [[October 2023 Speaker of the United States House of Representatives election]], as well as his stated willingness to compromise with House Minority Leader [[Hakeem Jeffries]] to elect a different candidate.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://1819news.com/news/item/rogers-draws-rebuke-from-conservatives-after-signaling-willingness-to-cut-deal-with-dems-to-resolve-u-s-house-speaker-impasse|title=Rogers draws rebuke from conservatives after signaling willingness to cut deal with Dems to resolve U.S. House Speaker impasse|last=Poor|first=Jeff|work=1819 News|date=October 15, 2023|access-date=October 16, 2023}}</ref> In response, members of the Alabama Republican Party state executive committee, including members from the 3rd district, threatened to file a challenge against Rogers' ballot access in the 2024 election.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://1819news.com/news/item/algop-executive-committee-member-threatens-republican-primary-ballot-access-challenge-against-u-s-rep-rogers-over-house-speaker-saga|title=ALGOP executive committee member threatens Republican primary ballot access challenge against U.S. Rep. Rogers over House Speaker saga|last=Poor|first=Jeff|work=1819 News|date=October 16, 2023|access-date=October 16, 2023}}</ref> On October 16, 2023, Rogers issued a statement endorsing Jordan for Speaker of the House, reversing his position and establishing his support for Jordan.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.al.com/news/2023/10/alabamas-mike-rogers-will-back-jim-jordan-for-house-speaker-i-have-always-been-a-team-player.html|title=Alabama's Mike Rogers will back Jim Jordan for House Speaker: 'I have always been a team player'|last=Thornton|first=William|work=AL.com|date=October 16, 2023|access-date=October 16, 2023}}</ref>

No Democratic candidates qualified to run in this district, though Rogers faced two unsuccessful primary challengers.<ref name="WhoALNov">{{Cite web|url=https://www.al.com/news/2023/11/whos-running-in-alabamas-redrawn-2nd-congressional-district-other-districts.html|title=Who's running? 21 candidates join race in Alabama's redrawn 2nd Congressional District|last=Cason|first=Mike|date=November 10, 2023|access-date=November 12, 2023}}</ref>

